## Phishing Attack Case Study

Phishing is a type of cybercrime where the  attackers trick users into revealing the  sensitive information such as passwords or bank details.
 It usually happens through fake emails or messages that appear to be from trusted sources.
A common scenario involves a user receiving an email claiming to be from a bank. 
The email asks the user to click on a link and update account details then  link leads to a fake website that looks real.
 When the user enters their credentials, the attacker gains access.
Students and working professionals are often targeted due to lack of awareness. The consequences include financial loss, identity theft, and data breaches.

This highlights the importance of verifying links and avoiding suspicious emails.